{
  "id": "dynamic-assessment",
  "term": "dynamic assessment",
  "definition": "Dynamic assessment is an approach to evaluation, based in Vygotsky’s sociocultural theory, that looks at a learner’s developmental potential by examining how they perform when guided or supported. It focuses on learning within the zone of proximal development rather than only on what the person can do independently.",
